:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKUSRPRF HELP=HLPWRK KEYL=WRKKEYS TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with User Profiles
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=USERS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?CRTUSRPRF USRPRF(&WUPNAME.)'.1=Create
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGUSRPRF USRPRF(&WUPNAME.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD DLTUSRPRF USRPRF(&WUPNAME.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPUSRPRF USRPRF(&WUPNAME.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT OPTION=12 ENTER='CMD WRKOBJOWN USRPRF(&WUPNAME.)'.12=Work with objects by owner
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=WUPNAME USAGE=OUTPUT.User Profile
:LISTCOL VAR=WUPCLS USAGE=OUTPUT.User Class
:LISTCOL VAR=WUPTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPDSP.Display User Profile - Help
:P.This display shows a user profile: how its owner signs on, the
password rules that apply to it, its class and special authorities,
its groups and the defaults its jobs start with.
:P.Page down for the rest of the attributes. Press Enter, F3 or F12
to leave. CHGUSRPRF changes them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPWRK.Work with User Profiles - Help
:P.This display lists the user profiles on the system with their class
and text.
:P.Type an option next to a profile and press Enter: 2 changes it, 4
deletes it, 5 shows it and 12 lists the objects it owns. F6 creates a
new profile.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
